Requirements: 28   with obligations: 27   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] Make the cost of a run attributable to the stage that incurred it. Every model
    call the review pipeline issues records which stage issued it, how many tokens it
    used, what it cost, and how much of its prompt the provider served from cache. At
    the end of a run the tool reports that breakdown stage by stage, keeping what the
    run itself spent separate from what its evidence cost when that evidence was first
    recorded.
    -> stage-attributed-run-cost  [functional/explicit]
       A run's cost is attributable to the stage that incurred it.
    -> model-call-stage-usage-cost-cache-recording  [functional/explicit]
       Every model call the review pipeline issues records which stage issued it, how
       many tokens it used, what it cost, and how much of its prompt the provider served
       from cache.
    -> run-report-stage-breakdown  [functional/explicit]
       At the end of a run the tool reports the breakdown stage by stage, keeping what
       the run itself spent separate from what its evidence cost when that evidence was
       first recorded.

[constraint-01] Every model call the review pipeline issues records the stage that
    issued it.
    -> call-records-issuing-stage  [functional/explicit]
       Every model call the review pipeline issues records the stage that issued it.

[constraint-02] No model call the review pipeline issues reports its stage as unknown.
    -> call-stage-never-unknown  [invariant/explicit]
       No model call the review pipeline issues reports its stage as unknown.

[constraint-03] Recorded usage carries the cached-token counts the provider reports
    alongside the prompt token count.
    -> record-usage-includes-cached-token-counts  [functional/explicit]
       Recorded usage carries the cached-token counts the provider reports alongside the
       prompt token count.

[constraint-04] A cached-token count the provider does not report is absent from the
    recorded usage rather than recorded as zero.
    -> cached-token-count-absent-when-unreported  [functional/explicit]
       A cached-token count the provider does not report is absent from recorded usage
       rather than represented as zero.

[constraint-05] A call answered from a recording is observed with the same fields as a
    call answered by the provider.
    -> recorded-call-matches-provider-call-fields  [invariant/explicit]
       A call answered from a recording is observed with the same fields as a call
       answered by the provider.

[constraint-06] Each observed call records the stage that issued it, its request key,
    whether it was answered from a recording or by the provider, and its usage.
    -> observed-call-records-stage-request-key-source-and-usage  [functional/explicit]
       Each observed call records the stage that issued it, its request key, whether it
       was answered from a recording or by the provider, and its usage.

[constraint-07] A run reports tokens, cost and cached prompt-token share for each stage
    that issued a call.
    -> run-reports-stage-breakdown-metrics  [functional/explicit]
       A run reports tokens, cost and cached prompt-token share for each stage that
       issued a call.

[constraint-08] The cached prompt-token share of a stage is the share of that stage's
    prompt tokens that the provider served from its cache.
    -> cached-prompt-token-share-definition  [functional/explicit]
       The cached prompt-token share of a stage is the share of that stage's prompt
       tokens that the provider served from its cache.

[constraint-09] A run's report distinguishes calls answered by the provider from calls
    answered from a recording.
    -> run-report-distinguishes-provider-from-recording-calls  [functional/explicit]
       A run's report distinguishes calls answered by the provider from calls answered
       from a recording.

[constraint-10] The cost reported for a call answered from a recording is what that call
    cost when it was recorded.
    -> recorded-call-cost-reflects-recording-time-cost  [functional/explicit]
       The cost reported for a call answered from a recording is what that call cost
       when it was recorded.

[constraint-11] The amount a run reports as its own spend counts only calls answered by
    the provider.
    -> run-own-spend-counts-provider-calls-only  [functional/explicit]
       The amount a run reports as its own spend counts only calls answered by the
       provider.

[constraint-12] The command-line interface surfaces the breakdown.
    -> cli-surfaces-breakdown  [functional/explicit]
       The command-line interface surfaces the stage-by-stage cost breakdown.

[constraint-13] Recording the stage of a call leaves that call's request key unchanged.
    -> stage-recording-keeps-request-key  [invariant/explicit]
       Recording the stage of a call leaves that call's request key unchanged.

[constraint-14] Recording cached-token counts in a call's usage leaves that call's
    request key unchanged.
    -> cached-token-recording-keeps-request-key  [invariant/explicit]
       Recording cached-token counts in a call's usage leaves that call's request key
       unchanged.

[constraint-15] The breakdown appears in no review state.
    -> breakdown-absent-from-review-state  [regression/explicit]
       The breakdown appears in no review state.

[constraint-16] The breakdown appears in no rendered report.
    -> breakdown-absent-from-rendered-report  [regression/explicit]
       The breakdown appears in no rendered report.

[exclusion-01] Any work to make a run cheaper, and any work to increase how much of a
    prompt the provider serves from its cache.
    -> no-run-cheaper-or-more-cache-work  [regression/explicit]
       The change does not include work to make a run cheaper or to increase how much of
       a prompt the provider serves from its cache.

[exclusion-02] Attributing cost to anything finer than the stage that issued the call.
    -> no-finer-than-stage-cost-attribution  [invariant/explicit]
       The change does not attribute cost to anything finer than the stage that issued
       the call.

[exclusion-03] Model calls issued by the measurement harness, which is not part of a
    review run.
    -> exclude-measurement-harness-calls  [compatibility/explicit]
       Model calls issued by the measurement harness are not part of a review run.

[exclusion-04] Recording what a call cost at any moment other than when the call was
    made.
    -> no-cost-recording-at-other-time  [regression/explicit]
       The change does not record what a call cost at any moment other than when the
       call was made.

[exclusion-05] Computing the price of a token, which the provider's own accounting
    already reports for each call.
    -> no-token-price-computation  [regression/explicit]
       The change does not compute the price of a token beyond the provider's own
       accounting for each call.

[exclusion-06] Presenting the breakdown anywhere other than the command line.
    -> cli-only-breakdown-presentation  [compatibility/explicit]
       The breakdown is presented only on the command line.

[completion-01] Implementation
    -- no obligation, deliberately
       The bullet is a section marker naming the implementation section and does not
       itself state a checkable requirement.

[completion-02] A run reports tokens, cost and cached prompt-token share by stage, with
    calls answered by the provider distinguished from calls answered from a recording.
    -> stage-breakdown-report-by-stage  [functional/explicit]
       A run reports tokens, cost, and cached prompt-token share by stage, and
       distinguishes calls answered by the provider from calls answered from a
       recording.

[completion-03] A test fails when a model call site in the review pipeline omits the
    stage that issued it.
    -> test-fails-when-stage-omitted  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test fails when a model call site in the review pipeline omits the stage that
       issued it.

[completion-04] A test pins that recording usage fields leaves every request key
    unchanged.
    -> test-request-key-unchanged-for-recording-usage  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test pins that recording usage fields leaves every request key unchanged.

[completion-05] Two recorded runs over the same input produce byte-identical review
    state and byte-identical report output.
    -> byte-identical-repeated-recorded-runs  [regression/explicit]
       Two recorded runs over the same input produce byte-identical review state and
       byte-identical report output.
